<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Kianja</h1><p class="st-meta">1800 CE – 1963 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Haya kingdom near Bukoba, split from Kyamutwara around 1800, whose king Kahigi became a leading ally of German rule.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Kianja was formed around 1800 when succession disputes divided the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kyamutwara">Kingdom of Kyamutwara</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kagera-region">Kagera region</a> west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-victoria">Lake Victoria</a>. A branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinda-dynasty">Hinda dynasty</a> took control of the new kingdom, which became one of the largest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haya-people">Haya</a> states.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The mukama ruled over a dense population of banana and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> farmers through chiefs drawn from royal and noble lineages. In the 1890s King Kahigi II welcomed the Germans and used their support to extend his power over neighbouring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haya-people">Haya</a> states, a policy that made Kianja the most favoured native authority in the region.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Kianja remained a native authority under <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/german-east-africa">German East Africa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanganyika-territory">British Tanganyika Territory</a>. It ceased to exist in 1963, when independent <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tanganyika">Tanganyika</a> abolished the chieftaincies.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1800 CE – 1963 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Horn and East Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:95.52%;width:3.24%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1800 CE – 1963 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kahigi II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional religion, later Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Haya</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Tanzania</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kianja</dd></dl></aside></div>
